<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 57 in June.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 57 in June.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders (NAHB) said its Housing Market Index rose to 57 in June from a revised 55 in May.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales rose to 61 from a revised 59 in May, NAHB said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, traffic of prospective buyers held steady at 44 in June. And the component index for single-family sales in the next six months rose to 66 from a revised 64 during the same period.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The June index is based on the ratings of 402 respondents.  </p>
